BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_314970725@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260530T041218Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T153000
SUMMARY:So many trails in one hike!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meetup location: Silver Cre
 ek Trail head**\n**13479 Fallbrook Trail\, Ballinafad**\n**coordinates - 4
 3 41'31. 6"N**\n**-79 58'00. 7"W**\n\nHi All: Please join us as we travers
 e a number of trails. Bennet Heritage Trail\, Irwin Quarry and Robert Side
  Rd. Considered a moderately challenging hike folks so come with good hiki
 ng shoes\, and always come with rain gear cause no matter what\, we hike i
 n heat\, rain\, sleet or snow.\nLocated in Silver Creek Conservation Area 
 near Halton Hills\, this complex network traverses one of the most ecologi
 cally diverse sections of the Niagara Escarpment. Historically\, this area
  was settled by the Bennett family and later protected to preserve the Cre
 dit River headwaters. Geologically\, the Great Esker trail follows a rare 
 glacial ridge of sand and gravel formed by a meltwater river under ancient
  ice. The forest is a lush mix of sugar maple and hemlock\, home to white-
 tailed deer and spotted salamanders. The terrain is technical and rugged\,
  featuring steep rocky inclines\, limestone crevices\, and muddy lowland s
 ections.\nHikers recommend waterproof boots for the Silver Creek crossings
  and mention the esker provides unique elevated views. P
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/314970725/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260527T012908Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T012908Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_314474853@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260530T041218Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T160000
SUMMARY:Another Opportunity to Learn New Skills - Trekker Training
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meet up Point:** Algonquin 
 Park - Maggie Lake Entrance\n**Two Days...sat and sun**\n**Fee for Trekkin
 g Training: $99.**\n\nBecause it was so much fun\, we are offering Trekker
  Training again in June!\nWe want you (and all our members) out Trekking. 
 Don't give up your Sunday hikes\, but hey it's time to up your hiking game
 !\nWhich is why we are offering skills training for future trekkers so the
 y can join in on trekking adventures outside of Ontario.\nThere is a lot t
 o learn to prepare for a multi day trekk\, and we want you to be prepared.
  It is not just knowing what equipment to buy\, how much to carry\, tent s
 et up\, it's also food prep\, attitude\, and emergency skills and so much 
 more!\nSo\, in order for you to ensure you have a safe and the very BEST t
 rekking experience we are offering an overnight training experience.\n**Ex
 perienced Boots Trekkers feel free to hop in and show them how it's done!*
 *\nWe will cover in one weekend -\n\n* your weighted pack\n* pack pacing\n
 * water filtering\n* trail etiquette\n* safety\n* equipment must haves\n* 
 first aid\n* atittude adjustment\n* fire starting\n* navigation\n* ...and 
 more
